<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="generated_at" content="{{ ctx.generated_at.isoformat() }}">
<title>Chat-box-auto-open Experiment — A/B Analysis</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --fg: #1f2937;
    --muted: #6b7280;
    --line: #e5e7eb;
    --accent-A: {{ variant_colors["A"] }};
    --accent-B: {{ variant_colors["B"] }};
    --good: #d1fae5;
    --bad: #fee2e2;
    --warn: #fef3c7;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body {
    margin: 0; padding: 0;
    background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg);
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  main { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px; }
  h1 { font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 8px 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 32px 0 12px 0; padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); }
  h3 { font-size: 18px; margin: 20px 0 8px 0; color: var(--fg); }
  p { margin: 8px 0; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 8px 10px; text-align: right; }
  th { background: #f9fafb; text-align: left; }
  td:first-child, th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: #fafafa; }
  .verdict { font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .verdict-ship { background: var(--good); color: #065f46; }
  .verdict-do_not_ship { background: var(--bad); color: #991b1b; }
  .verdict-inconclusive { background: var(--warn); color: #92400e; }
  .sig-positive { background: var(--good); }
  .sig-negative { background: var(--bad); }
  .chart { margin: 12px 0 24px 0; }
  .grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  footer { margin-top: 48px; padding: 16px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .swatch-A { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; background: var(--accent-A); border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }
  .swatch-B { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px; background: var(--accent-B); border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }
</style>
<script>{{ plotly_bundle|safe }}</script>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<h1>Chat-box-auto-open Experiment — A/B Analysis</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Date range: {{ ctx.date_range[0].strftime('%Y-%m-%d') }} → {{ ctx.date_range[1].strftime('%Y-%m-%d') }}
  · <span class="swatch-A"></span>Variant A (control, manual-open)
  · <span class="swatch-B"></span>Variant B (treatment, auto-open)
</p>

{# ============== EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ============== #}
<section id="exec-summary">
<h2>Executive Summary</h2>
<p><strong>Recommendation:</strong>
  {% if ctx.exec_summary.recommendation == "ship" %}
    <span class="verdict verdict-ship">SHIP</span>
  {% elif ctx.exec_summary.recommendation == "do_not_ship" %}
    <span class="verdict verdict-do_not_ship">DO NOT SHIP</span>
  {% else %}
    <span class="verdict verdict-inconclusive">INCONCLUSIVE — needs more data</span>
  {% endif %}
</p>
<p>{{ ctx.exec_summary.headline_engagement }}</p>
<p>{{ ctx.exec_summary.headline_redirect }}</p>
<p><em>{{ ctx.exec_summary.rationale }}</em></p>
</section>

{# ============== DATA OVERVIEW ============== #}
<section id="data-overview">
<h2>Data Overview</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Rows loaded</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>ots_chat.csv</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.chat_rows) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>redirects.csv</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.redirect_rows) }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Distinct utids in ots_chat</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>A (control)</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.variant_population.A) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>B (auto-open)</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.variant_population.B) }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
{% if ctx.excluded_utids_count > 0 %}
<p class="muted">{{ ctx.excluded_utids_count }} utid(s) excluded due to in-file variant conflict.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

{# ============== ENGAGEMENT ============== #}
<section id="engagement">
<h2>Engagement Analysis</h2>
<p class="muted">Engagement metrics: 2 chat_types × 4 aggregation dimensions = 8 metrics. Rate = distinct dimension count / variant_population.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Chat type</th><th>Dimension</th>
      <th>A count</th><th>B count</th>
      <th>A rate</th><th>B rate</th>
      <th>Δ rate</th><th>Rel. lift</th>
      <th>p-value</th><th>95% CI for Δ</th>
      <th>Verdict</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for m in ctx.engagement_metrics %}
    <tr {% if m.significance_verdict == "significant" and m.directional_verdict == "positive" %}class="sig-positive"{% elif m.significance_verdict == "significant" and m.directional_verdict == "negative" %}class="sig-negative"{% endif %}>
      <td>{{ m.chat_type }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.dimension }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.count_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.count_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.value_A|fmt_num(4) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.value_B|fmt_num(4) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.abs_diff|fmt_num(4) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.p_value|fmt_p }}</td>
      <td>[{{ m.ci_low|fmt_num(4) }}, {{ m.ci_high|fmt_num(4) }}]</td>
      <td>{{ m.directional_verdict }} / {{ m.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="grid-2">
  {% for m in ctx.engagement_metrics %}
    <div class="chart">{{ engagement_charts[m.chat_type ~ '__' ~ m.dimension]|safe }}</div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>

<h3>Rounds per session (Welch's t-test)</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Variant</th><th>n sessions</th><th>Mean</th><th>Median</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>A</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.rounds_metric.n_sessions_A) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.mean_A|fmt_num(2) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.median_A|fmt_num(2) }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>B</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.rounds_metric.n_sessions_B) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.mean_B|fmt_num(2) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.rounds_metric.median_B|fmt_num(2) }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Δ mean = {{ ctx.rounds_metric.abs_diff_mean|fmt_num(3) }} ·
   relative lift = {{ ctx.rounds_metric.rel_lift_mean_pct|fmt_lift }} ·
   p = {{ ctx.rounds_metric.p_value|fmt_p }} ·
   95% CI = [{{ ctx.rounds_metric.ci_low|fmt_num(3) }}, {{ ctx.rounds_metric.ci_high|fmt_num(3) }}] ·
   {{ ctx.rounds_metric.directional_verdict }} / {{ ctx.rounds_metric.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</p>
<div class="chart">{{ rounds_chart_html|safe }}</div>

<h3>Daily trend — engagement absolute (INTENT_RECOGNITION volume)</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["engagement_abs"]|safe }}</div>

<h3>Daily trend — engagement ratio (INTENT_RECOGNITION ÷ SUGGESTIONS)</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["engagement_ratio"]|safe }}</div>
</section>

{# ============== REDIRECT ============== #}
<section id="redirect">
<h2>Redirect Analysis</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Redirect rates are computed only over CHAT_TYPE_INTENT_RECOGNITION rows (FR-009).
  Numerator: distinct dimension values that match a redirect via correlation_id ↔ pre_redirect_id.
  Denominator: distinct dimension values in INTENT-only chat data.
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Dimension</th>
      <th>A num</th><th>A den</th><th>A rate</th>
      <th>B num</th><th>B den</th><th>B rate</th>
      <th>Δ (pp)</th><th>Rel. lift</th>
      <th>p-value</th><th>95% CI for Δ</th>
      <th>Verdict</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for m in ctx.redirect_metrics %}
    <tr {% if m.significance_verdict == "significant" and m.directional_verdict == "positive" %}class="sig-positive"{% elif m.significance_verdict == "significant" and m.directional_verdict == "negative" %}class="sig-negative"{% endif %}>
      <td>{{ m.dimension }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_A) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_A|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.numerator_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ "{:,}".format(m.denominator_B) }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rate_B|fmt_pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.abs_diff|fmt_pp }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.p_value|fmt_p }}</td>
      <td>[{{ m.ci_low|fmt_pp }}, {{ m.ci_high|fmt_pp }}]</td>
      <td>{{ m.directional_verdict }} / {{ m.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Funnel rate — redirect rate over all chat users (FR-013)</h3>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Numerator</th><th>Denominator (utids in ots_chat)</th><th>Rate</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>A</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.numerator_A) }}</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.denominator_A) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.rate_A|fmt_pct }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>B</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.numerator_B) }}</td><td>{{ "{:,}".format(ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.denominator_B) }}</td><td>{{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.rate_B|fmt_pct }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Δ = {{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.abs_diff|fmt_pp }} ·
   relative lift = {{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.rel_lift_pct|fmt_lift }} ·
   p = {{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.p_value|fmt_p }} ·
   95% CI = [{{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.ci_low|fmt_pp }}, {{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.ci_high|fmt_pp }}] ·
   {{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.directional_verdict }} / {{ ctx.redirect_funnel_metric.significance_verdict.replace('_', ' ') }}</p>

<div class="grid-2">
  {% for m in ctx.redirect_metrics %}
    <div class="chart">{{ redirect_charts['redirect__' ~ m.dimension]|safe }}</div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="chart">{{ redirect_charts["redirect_funnel"]|safe }}</div>
</div>

<h3>Daily trend — redirect absolute</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["redirect_abs"]|safe }}</div>

<h3>Daily trend — redirect ratio (redirect ÷ INTENT_RECOGNITION)</h3>
<div class="chart">{{ trend_charts["redirect_ratio"]|safe }}</div>
</section>

{# ============== APPENDIX ============== #}
<section id="appendix">
<h2>Appendix</h2>

<h3>Methodology</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Engagement rate:</strong> distinct dimension count / variant_population (utids in ots_chat).</li>
  <li><strong>Engagement ratio (trend chart 2):</strong> at the utid panel — distinct INTENT utids / distinct SUGGESTIONS utids per (dt, variant). At the chat_session_id panel, since SUGGESTIONS rows have empty session_id, the denominator is the SUGGESTIONS row count per (dt, variant) — interpretable as "INTENT sessions started per suggestion render".</li>
  <li><strong>Redirect attribution:</strong> a chat row is "redirected" iff its correlation_id appears in redirects.pre_redirect_id (FR-010). Suggestions are excluded (FR-009).</li>
  <li><strong>Funnel rate:</strong> distinct utids with ≥1 attributed redirect ÷ variant_population (= distinct utids in ots_chat per variant). FR-013.</li>
  <li><strong>Statistical tests:</strong> two-proportion z-test for rate metrics; Welch's t-test for the rounds mean. α = {{ ctx.alpha }}. Two-sided.</li>
  <li><strong>Directional verdict:</strong> a relative lift greater than +{{ ctx.flat_threshold_pct }}% is "positive"; less than −{{ ctx.flat_threshold_pct }}% is "negative"; otherwise "flat" (FR-007).</li>
  <li><strong>Significance verdict:</strong> "significant" iff p &lt; {{ ctx.alpha }} (FR-SIG-004).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Multiple comparisons</h3>
<p>
  This report runs <strong>{{ ctx.total_tests }}</strong> two-sided tests in total at α = {{ ctx.alpha }}.
  At this multiplicity, the expected number of false positives under the null hypothesis is approximately
  <strong>{{ "%.2f"|format(ctx.expected_false_positives) }}</strong>. No multiple-comparisons correction
  (Bonferroni / Benjamini-Hochberg) is applied (FR-SIG-006). Treat borderline-significant findings
  with this in mind.
</p>

<h3>Excluded data</h3>
<p>
  {% if ctx.excluded_utids_count == 0 %}
    No utids excluded.
  {% else %}
    {{ ctx.excluded_utids_count }} utid(s) excluded due to in-file variant conflict in ots_chat.csv.
  {% endif %}
  Cross-file variant validation (against actions.csv) is intentionally NOT performed in this analysis
  (per Clarifications session 2026-05-21).
</p>

<h3>Per-day per-variant row counts</h3>
<p class="muted">Sanity-check: for any day where one variant's row count is much smaller than the other, treat the daily-trend points with caution.</p>
{# We could render a small daily counts table here in a future iteration. #}

</section>

<footer>
  Generated {{ ctx.generated_at.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC') }}
  · Source: ots_chat.csv + redirects.csv
  · Plotly bundle inlined for offline viewing
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
